## General rule

When in doubt, drop the file into `raw/unsorted/`. The pipeline will classify it or queue it for review.

## Adding files through chat

If you attach a file directly in chat, the AI agent must ask before adding it to the main knowledge base:

1. Summarize the attached file(s) and propose the best `raw/<category>/unsorted/` destination
2. Ask: "Add this to the main knowledge base?"
3. Only after confirmation, stage the file into `raw/` and run `./shell/reindex.sh` or confirm the watcher processed it
4. If the file looks low-value or unrelated, ask whether to keep it as an asset, archive it, or ignore it

## Common cases

| You have | Put it in |
|----------|-----------|
| A PDF/DOCX strategy doc, report, presentation | `raw/documents/unsorted/` |
| An interesting article saved from the web | `raw/reference/unsorted/` |
| An exported chat (Telegram, Slack, Discord) | `raw/chats/unsorted/` |
| Audio/video recording (meeting, voice memo) | `raw/media/unsorted/` |
| Random notes, screenshots, drafts | `raw/unsorted/` |
| Personal context (history, preferences) | `raw/personal-context/unsorted/` |

## After dropping

1. (If watcher is running) — files are picked up a few seconds after they stop changing
2. (Manual) — run `./shell/reindex.sh` to trigger the pipeline
3. Check `STATUS.md` (what is waiting, and the command that resolves it) and `log.md` (what happened)
4. Say `!review` — the AI agent works through the `review/` queues and the `processed/` items still waiting for extraction, and writes `knowledge/` pages
5. Check `knowledge/` to see freshly extracted knowledge

## What NOT to drop

- Secrets, API tokens, private keys, banking data
- Third-party private chats without explicit permission
- Medical or legal data of others
- Material that would be embarrassing or harmful if leaked

By default (the `privacy:` section of `kb.config.yml`), chats, personal context
and files in which the pipeline spots credential-looking strings go to
`review/needs-redaction/` first. You can also place a sensitive file there manually.

